And Esmeralda says, listen, getting these original stories is expensive.

1342
00:56:29.910 --> 00:56:32.650
I think we need to go back to the way it was before Ned.

1343
00:56:33.350 --> 00:56:37.410
Yeah, basically, she's like, Ned's idea to do original stories was a bad idea.

1344
00:56:37.410 --> 00:56:39.470
She's, again, trying to throw him under the bus.

1345
00:56:39.630 --> 00:56:42.110
She says they should pay for the wire stories.

1346
00:56:42.570 --> 00:56:48.990
But then Oscar brings up a line item that he found in the budget that's a little curious.

1347
00:56:49.230 --> 00:56:55.670
It's a storage unit that they've been renting for nine years that's actually an apartment.

1348
00:56:56.430 --> 00:57:00.770
Yeah, so in the Peacock version, you guys, it's extended.

1349
00:57:00.830 --> 00:57:07.730
And you sort of see Oscar really struggling because he knows Esmeralda and Ken are trying to sabotage Ned.

1350
00:57:07.910 --> 00:57:08.110
Yeah.

1351
00:57:08.110 --> 00:57:14.370
And you can also tell that Oscar maybe believes in Ned and thinks he should stick around and not get fired.

1352
00:57:14.550 --> 00:57:14.770
Yeah.

1353
00:57:15.010 --> 00:57:18.310
So he decides to play this card to save the day.

1354
00:57:18.590 --> 00:57:18.730
Yeah.

1355
00:57:18.770 --> 00:57:19.290
To save Ned.

1356
00:57:19.610 --> 00:57:26.610
We find out that this storage unit, quote unquote, that's actually an apartment, is Ken's apartment.

1357
00:57:26.610 --> 00:57:34.550
He has a talking head where he says, yeah, Enervate rented him a small furnished apartment for a few weeks when he first moved over from the UK.

1358
00:57:35.550 --> 00:57:38.810
And somehow it got filed as a warehouse.

1359
00:57:39.110 --> 00:57:40.170
Ah, could you imagine?

1360
00:57:40.710 --> 00:57:41.050
Mm-hmm.

1361
00:57:41.310 --> 00:57:48.490
So he's been sneaky sneak living rent-free and billing it back to the company as a storage facility.

1362
00:57:49.030 --> 00:57:51.730
So back in the meeting, Ken's like, you know what?

1363
00:57:51.970 --> 00:57:53.890
Let's get rid of this storage unit.

1364
00:57:54.130 --> 00:57:56.010
No need to investigate what happened.

1365
00:57:56.330 --> 00:57:57.630
That's a waste of money.

1366
00:57:57.890 --> 00:57:58.870
But look at that.

1367
00:57:58.870 --> 00:58:01.690
We'll have the money back in the budget and journalism wins.

1368
00:58:02.150 --> 00:58:04.950
And then we have just some wrap-up moments, you know.

1369
00:58:05.070 --> 00:58:09.310
So basically, Esmeralda knows that she's been beat once again.

1370
